{
  "anonymous": false,
  "paper": {
    "title": "MIRROR: Motion-Internalized Reasoning with Reciprocal On-Policy Reinforcement for Unified Motion Generation and Understanding",
    "abstract": "Unified motion generation and understanding models jointly address text-to-motion generation and motion-to-text understanding. However, existing methods rely on explicit textual Chain-of-Thought (CoT) reasoning and task-specific reinforcement learning. Explicit CoT overlooks fine-grained kinematics and adds autoregressive overhead, while independent rewards limit cross-task feedback. We propose MIRROR, combining Motion-Internalized Reasoning (MIR) and Reciprocal On-Policy Reinforcement (ROR). MIR learns semantic and kinematic latent reasoning states that implicitly encode textual reasoning and phase-wise motion signatures, enabling reasoning entirely during prompt prefill. ROR couples both tasks through reciprocal on-policy cycles, allowing generation and understanding to improve each other during training. Extensive experiments show that MIRROR achieves state-of-the-art performance among unified models in both motion generation and understanding.",
